From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:48:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: leave inactive keyboard columns
 undriven

With drive-inactive-cols, the matrix scan drives the selected AW9523
column low and every other column high. Two pressed keys in the same row
then join a low column to a high one. The row sits between the two and
reads as released, so both keys disappear.

The named unit shows this. With the station kernel and an event capture,
holding Left Shift (row 3, column 6) and pressing Z (row 3, column 0)
reported Shift released and never reported Z; Shift returned once Z was
released. Right Shift+Z and Left Shift+Q were reported correctly.
Ctrl+Alt behaves the same, since both are in row 4. Every Left Shift
capital in row 3 (Z, X, C, V, B, N) and every Ctrl or Alt combination
with another row-4 key is therefore lost.

Drop drive-inactive-cols so the scan turns inactive columns into inputs.
A pressed key then only connects its row to the one driven column. The
cost is the usual one for an undiodded matrix: three keys on the corners
of a rectangle produce a phantom fourth. The ghost filter already enabled
on this node drops those scans.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
index 337aac1d5..48aee99ad 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -468,8 +468,10 @@ keyboard-matrix {
 		compatible = "gpio-matrix-keypad";
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		gpio-activelow;
-		drive-inactive-cols;
-		/* No per-key diodes: Ctrl+Left Shift+N also reads M. */
+		/*
+		 * Inactive columns stay undriven: driving them high makes two
+		 * keys in one row cancel. No per-key diodes, so filter ghosts.
+		 */
 		needs-ghost-filter;
 		pinctrl-0 = <&keyboard_matrix_row_pins
 				     &keyboard_matrix_col_pins>;
